================================================================================
npm dependencies
================================================================================

Backspace depends on open-source packages distributed via npm, all under
permissive licenses (predominantly MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0, and BSD variants).
The image-processing dependency "sharp" loads libvips, distributed as a
prebuilt binary under the LGPL-3.0-or-later license; it is used unmodified and
dynamically, and is not statically linked into Backspace.

The desktop app on Linux optionally depends on "@vencord/venmic"
(https://github.com/Vencord/venmic), a prebuilt native PipeWire module distributed
via npm under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0). It routes other
applications' audio into a virtual source for screen sharing (packages/desktop/src/
systemAudio.ts). It is used unmodified, as a separate file-level component; its
source code is available at the address above and the license text ships in the
package's LICENSE file. Its dependencies that are installed, node-addon-api and
pkg-prebuilds, are MIT; its build tool cmake-js is not installed.

To regenerate the full, current dependency license inventory, run:

  pnpm licenses list --prod

================================================================================
Camera backgrounds
================================================================================

The camera backgrounds (packages/web/src/camera/) find the person in the picture
with Google's MediaPipe, through LiveKit's track processors:

@livekit/track-processors
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (https://github.com/livekit/track-processors-js)
  An npm dependency, used unmodified.

@mediapipe/tasks-vision
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe)
  Its JavaScript is bundled; its WebAssembly (vision_wasm_internal.js and
  vision_wasm_internal.wasm) is copied unmodified from the package into the
  build under /mediapipe/<version>/ (packages/web/src/build/visionAssets.mjs).

MediaPipe Selfie Segmentation model
  File:     packages/web/src/camera/selfie_segmenter.tflite (float16, square)
  License:  Apache License 2.0, as stated in its model card
            (https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/Model%20Card%20MediaPipe%20Selfie%20Segmentation.pdf)
  Notice:   Copyright Google LLC
  Downloaded unmodified from
  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/image_segmenter/selfie_segmenter/float16/latest/selfie_segmenter.tflite

The text of the Apache License 2.0 is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.

The scenes in packages/web/src/camera/scenes/ are drawn by scripts/camera-scenes/
for Tavvit and are covered by the project license.

